<title>USA: First Federal Ky. starts shr repurchase.</title>
<headline>First Federal Ky. starts shr repurchase.</headline>
<dateline>ELIZABETHTOWN, Ky. 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>First Federal Financial Corp of Kentucky said Tuesday it is starting a stock repurchase program to buy back up to 5 percent of its outstanding common shares.</p>
<p>It said the 18-month plan would be dependent upon market conditions and SEC regulations, with no guarantee as to the number of shares to be repurchased.</p>
<p>The corporation is a $377 million family financial services holding company serving central Kentucky.</p>
</text>
